{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>מושל</b> — The word עולם throughout all of Scripture means only a duration or eternity. The sense: that HaShem rules forever, like מושל נצח, in the greatness of His might, and His dominion over the nations whom He watches. For it is not sound for the bet in בגבורתו to be like 'משל בנו' (ruled over us), for that has no meaning. Behold, He stated that His dominion is over sea and dry land; therefore the rebellious who defy Him shall not be exalted."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:52.054296416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}